   "source": [
    "## Usage Instructions and Next Steps\n",
    "\n",
    "### Data Setup Requirements:\n",
    "\n",
    "1. **Directory Structure**: Create the following folder structure in your project:\n",
    "   ```\n",
    "   your-project/\n",
    "   ├── data/\n",
    "   │   ├── ISIC_2019_data/\n",
    "   │   │   └── combined_df_ISIC_2019.xlsx\n",
    "   │   ├── MIDAS_excel.xlsx\n",
    "   │   ├── Midas_photos_data/\n",
    "   │   │   └── [image files]\n",
    "   │   └── not_lesion_images/\n",
    "   │       └── [non-lesion image files]\n",
    "   ├── processed_data/\n",
    "   │   └── [generated outputs]\n",
    "   └── skin_cancer_preprocessing.ipynb\n",
    "   ```\n",
    "\n",
    "2. **Data Sources**:\n",
    "   - **ISIC 2019**: International Skin Imaging Collaboration dataset\n",
    "   - **MIDAS**: Medical imaging dataset with clinical annotations\n",
    "   - **Non-lesion images**: Background/control images without skin lesions\n",
    "\n",
    "3. **Output Files**:\n",
    "   - `processed_skin_lesion_data.pkl`: Complete dataset (recommended for Python)\n",
    "   - `processed_skin_lesion_data.csv`: CSV format (broader compatibility)\n",
    "   - `dataset_metadata.txt`: Dataset summary and statistics\n",
    "\n",
    "### Classification System:\n",
    "\n",
    "- **Label 0 - Melanoma Detected**: Confirmed melanoma cases\n",
    "- **Label 1 - Other Skin Cancer Detected**: BCC, SCC, AK, and other malignancies\n",
    "- **Label 2 - Benign Skin Lesion Detected**: Moles, keratoses, and other benign lesions\n",
    "- **Label 3 - No Concerning Lesion Detected**: Normal skin or non-lesion images\n",
    "\n",
    "### Next Steps for Model Development:\n",
    "\n",
    "1. **Load processed data**: Use the generated pickle file\n",
    "2. **Image preprocessing**: Implement data augmentation and normalization\n",
    "3. **Model architecture**: Design CNN/Vision Transformer for classification\n",
    "4. **Training pipeline**: Split data, train model, validate performance\n",
    "5. **Evaluation**: Use appropriate metrics for medical imaging (sensitivity, specificity)\n",
    "\n",
    "### Key Features Available:\n",
    "\n",
    "- **Image filenames**: For loading actual images\n",
    "- **Classification labels**: 4-class targets for training\n",
    "- **Demographic features**: Age and gender (normalized)\n",
    "- **Clinical information**: Original diagnoses and impressions\n",
    "- **Data source flags**: Distinguish between lesion/non-lesion images\n",
    "\n",
    "For questions or issues, please refer to the project documentation or open an issue in the repository."
   ]
